  "body": "According to the spec:\r\n\r\n```\r\nThe setTransform(transform) method, when invoked, must reset the current transformation \r\nmatrix to the value represented by the result of creating a DOMMatrix from a dictionary\r\ntransform, with ignore3D set to true.\r\n```\r\n\r\nPassing invalid values to `DOMMatrix` may result in an exception. It's not obvious from the spec wording if they should be re-thrown or ignored. Do we have an agreement on what's the correct behavior? And could we clarify the spec and language here? We should either say `...and re-throwing any exception` or say `... and ignoring the transform if creation throws`.\r\n\r\nAlso, we could remove `\"with ignore3D set to true\"`, since this is going away:\r\nhttps://github.com/w3c/fxtf-drafts/pull/218\r\n\r\nThis is somehow related to:\r\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/2845\r\n\r\n@zcorpan @junov @annevk @domenic @whatwg/canvas ",
